<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Apple's Privacy Manifest requirement is currently enforced for iOS/iPadOS/
  tvOS App Store submissions only — macOS apps are exempt as of this writing
  (see https://developer.apple.com/support/third-party-SDK-requirements/).
  Shipped anyway, ahead of that requirement, because it's free to be honest
  here and Apple has been widening manifest enforcement over time.

  OmniDB itself collects nothing and tracks nothing — every network
  connection it makes (database engines, SSH) is one the user explicitly
  configured, not telemetry back to us. NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes is left
  empty rather than guessed: attributing a "required reason" API declaration
  to a specific call inside the Go runtime or WKWebView (rather than this
  app's own code) isn't something this file's author could verify from the
  Go/Wails source alone. Revisit before ever shipping to a platform where
  the requirement is enforced (iOS/iPadOS/tvOS) or if Apple extends
  enforcement to macOS — `xcrun` will flag any real gap at submission time.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>NSPrivacyTracking</key>
	<false/>
	<key>NSPrivacyTrackingDomains</key>
	<array/>
	<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes</key>
	<array/>
	<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes</key>
	<array/>
</dict>
</plist>
